      "side": 1,
      "message": "Aseda, there are several calls which pass a variable length (probably to keep the overall loop time near a constant length). By accepting 0 as a valid length, callers don\u0027t need to check whether a wait is \u003e 0.\n\nI\u0027m not sure all the existing callers check wait \u003e 0. A bad thing about the current API behavior is that a bad call can cause a crash only randomly. As a matter of fact, I see some suspicious callers.\n\nSo, I think we should change the API so that it accepts 0 as a valid length. WDYT?",
